Undercurrent
============

(Formerly developed under the working name headlong-ts.)

This project is a TypeScript port of Headlong, the persistent-agent
microharness by the Laude Institute:

    https://github.com/laude-institute/headlong
    Copyright the Headlong authors.
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE).

Undercurrent is a best-effort, LLM-assisted reimplementation of Headlong's
deterministic behavior in TypeScript. It contains modifications from the
original and is NOT affiliated with or endorsed by the Laude Institute.

Provenance of the parts:

  - src/, web/server/   New TypeScript code written for this port. Where a
                        module ports a specific upstream unit, its header
                        cites the source (e.g. bin/shellm, bin/traj,
                        bin/thinkers, bin/mem, bin/skills, and the Python
                        modules under web/src/headlong_web/).

  - golden/, parity/    Behavioral oracle data captured by running the
                        original Headlong (Apache-2.0), used for the
                        differential tests described in PORTING.md. Demo
                        trajectory content has been de-identified.

  - web/viewer/         The original Headlong React viewer, vendored
                        (Apache-2.0) and unmodified except for a dev-server
                        proxy and npm scripts. See web/NOTICE and web/LICENSE
                        for the viewer's own provenance.

  - tui/                The original Headlong Rust terminal UI
                        (`headlong-tui`), vendored (Apache-2.0) and
                        unmodified. Per this port's Rust-stays-native rule,
                        the TUI is not reimplemented in TypeScript; it is
                        copied verbatim from headlong/tui and built with
                        cargo, shelling out to this port's `traj`, `chat`,
                        `thinkers`, `identity`, and `skills` CLIs on PATH.

The original work is licensed under Apache-2.0; this port is likewise
distributed under Apache-2.0 (see LICENSE).
